WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
Hot deserts lie along about
30 degrees north and south:

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:09.350
across northern Africa, Australia,
the American Southwest and Mexico.

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.490
Drylands cover about 46.2
per cent of the world's land.

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.230
Yet their hottest, driest
cores hold very few people.

5
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.590
Meanwhile, in South Asia, seasonal rains
water farmland crowded with people.

6
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.350
So does climate decide
where people live and farm?

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.770
Or do money and technology decide?

8
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.130
In this mission, you'll
map two climate types,

9
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.470
one hot and dry, one
with a sharp wet season,

10
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.410
and the people and farming each supports.

11
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.490
Then you'll see how climate
change is affecting farming,

12
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.810
in drylands and in lands of seasonal rain.

13
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.400
Your mission: decide whether climate
decides where people live and farm.
